{
  "id": "8e5b277b-397b-4a15-9c08-0e3a45758204",
  "type": "PARENT",
  "data": {
    "body": "A block of mass $M$ =  \\textbf{30 kg} is initially held at a certain point on an incline plane that makes an angle $\\theta = 48^\\circ$ as shown with the horizontal. The block is in contact with, but not attached to, a spring of stiffness, $k_s$ = $\\textbf{1200 N/m}$ and compressed length $L$ = $\\textbf{5.0 m}$. The relaxed length $L_0$ = $\\textbf{6.0 m}$ of the spring is also equal to the total length of the incline. When you release the block, the spring pushes it up all the way to the top of the incline, at which point it is launched into the air. \n\nThe coefficient of kinetic friction between the block and the incline plane is $\\mu_k$ = $\\textbf{0.3}.$ \n\nThe magnitude of acceleration due to gravity is g = 10 $m/s^2$",
    "numberingType": "NUMBER",
    "answerChoices": []
